  "result": "The real browser produced a valid three-frame slice ZIP with phases 0/0.5/1 and X slice positions 0/5/10 mm. The ZIP and all four STORE entries independently verified by CRC32 and SHA-256; all three PNGs decoded in the browser to 555 x 573 RGBA images with distinct pixel hashes. The official MCP startExport/exportStatus/exportArtifact/releaseExport path produced a byte-identical ZIP. The four states and section/camera controls were restored. Cancellation was terminal and refused the partial artifact. Invalid frame count, seconds with png-sequence, and stale revision were rejected. No source change was needed.",
  "unconfirmed": [
    "The browser is the OpenCode desktop Electron/Chromium build, not branded Google Chrome.",
    "Only localhost was used; public HTTPS, OS download and cross-origin deployment were not verified.",
    "Only one model and one successful three-frame export were checked. There is no multi-run distribution and no full-suite/post-push CI claim.",
    "The section-plane control was disabled initially; the result-view 'section' visibility flag was true. Both fields were restored and are recorded separately.",
    "The pixel hash is FNV-1a over decoded RGBA bytes, not a cryptographic hash; PNG and ZIP integrity use SHA-256. The decoder was the browser's createImageBitmap/canvas, not a Node PNG library.",
    "The cancellation request used 12 frames and was cancelled at 8.17%; other frame counts and cancellation timings were not exhaustively tested.",
    "The MCP path used inspect+view scopes because startExport is a view operation; the in-page path used the production visualExportApi directly.",
    "The parent BROWSEREXPORT1 unit remains incomplete; this is a bounded verification slice."
  ],
